        <head>LIVERPOOL.</head>
        <p>LIVERPOOL.</p>
        <p>competitor who succeeds in placing himself at the head of the Solvers' List at the end of the month. Where the prize is awarded the winner's score is cancelled, while the remaining competitors' points go towards the next month's competition. The win- ner may re-enter the competition if be chooses commencing again at the bottom of the list. Points are awarded as knows : Two for the correct solu- tion of a problem, two for showing a dual solution, two for correcting the author's terms, and one for each minor cOrrection.</p>
        <p>Intending c:.,mpetitors may commence at any time.</p>
        <p>SPECIAL NOTICE,</p>
        <p>With the advent of the New Year, we propose to alter the mode of scoring points in the abovo competition. Points will be awarded as follows Commencing with Problem No. 66 in our issue of January sth 1900. Two for the correct solution, of the Problem, two for correcting the authors' terms, one for showing a dual key move or a dual solution, and one for s'iowiul;,, a dual continuation at any stage of the solution.</p>
