        <p>No doubt our readers vvli notice that the Stock- ton Heath Club is conspicuous by its absence this season from the above tables. The club, owing to some friction arising with the officials at the Church Institute, Stockton Heath has been disbanded, but we are pleased to find that the players have re- formed themselves again into a club, and under the name of Latchford. are still coutnuing to "play with little bits of wood." They, however, not f,=.+l- ing competent to.combAt with the clubs of the Ist Division t his season have decided to enrol them- selves in the 2nd Division. Consequently this only 1, ayes fire clubs in the Ist Division, as against ix last season,</p>
