        <p>THE lIIATCR AT RUNCORN ABANDONED. Owing to the severe frost the match between Runcorn and Sr- ckport was abandoned last Saturday. Endeavours should. however, be made t_O get the match played-off on a Saturday, in preference to a Wednesdav, as Stock- port,bAng the only team which has successfully opposed "the linnets" this season, would ensure a record gate.</p>
        <p>"YOUNG MEN " AT THE MERSEY MISSION. The weekly concert at the Meney Mission was given entirely by a number of young men who veiled their identity behind . such names as" Wiese," " Andersh," " Schmidt," " two Macks," " Professor Froscati," etc. The programme which was unique was cipitally sus- tained and *appreciated by the large attendance present. The Chairman was Mr W Shaw (missioner).</p>
        <p>A DESERTER AT RUNCORN.</p>
