        <p>HOSPITAL ACCOMMaDATION.—NO ROOM AT CHESTER. Mr. S. Smith, town clerk, of Chester, wrote in reply to the Clerk's letter of the 6th imt., stating his com- mittee regretted the application for the reception of in- fectious cases at the Chester Hospital could nbt be en- tertained, their accommodation not being sufficient to admit of it. COMPLETION OF THE WESTON SEWERAGE WORKS. Mr. William Joynson, clerk of works, reported that Mr. Bennie had completed his contract for the extension of the sewer at Weston Point as per specification in a satisfactory manner.</p>
