      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-12-22_WidnesExaminer_art0077" n="art0077">
        <head>WARRINGTON.</head>
        <p>WARRINGTON.</p>
        <p>Personal. The Bishop of Chester has instituted the Rev. F. A. Screeton to the benefice of Christ Churcia,Latch- ford, and has licensed the Rev. S. W. Dunn to the assistant curacy of Daresbury. In a large entry of orpingtons, at Manchester poultry show, Messrs Reid and Hatton, of Bewsey, were highly commended with a single-comb black erpington cockerel.</p>
        <p>At the recent examination of the London College of Music, Liverpool centre, Edith A. Unsworth was successful in obtaining a first-class with honours in pianoforte playing, intermediate division. Mr. Frederick Pod more, pupil of Mr. J. B. Cald- well, has successfully passed with honours the senior examination in organ playing, of the London College of Music.</p>
        <p>Spiritualism.</p>
        <p>Mrs. Cropper occupied the platform at the Spirit- ualist Hall on Sunday, giving addresses on Summer-land" and "What must I do to be saved Both were succeeded by distinct clairvoyance. On Monday evening the same lady gave several illus- trations of mPdical prchometry and clairvoyance. __ _ _</p>
        <p>P.S,A. at the Y.M.C.A. The usual P.S.A. meeting was held in the lecture ball on Sunday afternoon, and was largely attended when Mr. Joseph Owen, of Blackpool, gave an address. Mr. Clough, one of the members,presided, and the President and Mr. Jones also took part is the meeting, which was very instructive and en. joyable.</p>
        <p>Eben ezer Church, Butterm arket-street. The band of hope meeting was ,held in the above place of worship on Monday evening, when there was a very good attendance. Mr E Little- wood occupied the chair. The programme consisted of the following: Solo, Miss A Grounds; ViOlill duet, Messrs. A Bennett and R W D Cook; dialogue, Miss B and N Bowyer and Miss B Thornley ; trios, Masters Grounds ; Irish sketch, Mr. Worrall ; solo, Miss Littlewood;violin solo,Mr. A Bennett; dialogue, " Mrs Maggs is caught," by the members of Hill Cliff Band of hope Society; solo, Miss Cissy Grounds ; recitation, M Whitfield; song, Mr lover; dialogue, " The Teetotal Barber," by Messrs R W Cooke, W Griffiths, N Cook, R W D Cook, E Littlewood, J Riley, R Lawson and Mrs Lee, Mr J A Thornton was the accompanist. The various items were greatly appreciated. The meet- ing was arranged by Mrs Bennett. A vote of thanks to the chairman and friends from Hill Cliff and Latchford brought a very successful meeting to a close.</p>
