        <p>BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON NOTICH IS lIHICHBY GIVRN That The Town Council o the Borough of Warrington have (subject to the approval of the Local Government Board) made certain Bylaw. in pursuance of the Publio Health Acts.as to the decent conduct of persons using Sanitacw Conveniences proviled and maintained by the Council for public accommodation, 2. A p.inted copy of the proposed Bylaws will continue deposited for inspection by any ratepayer, at the Office of the Town Clerk, at the Town Hall, for one calendar month from and a:ter the date of the first publication of this notice. 3. At the expirati,a of the said month the said proposed Bylaws will be submitted to the Local Government Board for approval and confirmation. 4. The Town C:erk will supply a printed copy of the said proposed Bylaws, or any part thereof, on application. Dated the 16th day of Dec.ember, 1899. J. LYON WHITTLE, Town Clerk.</p>
        <p>BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON.-NEW LAWS. IN • ERPRETATIONi. Street Musicians to depart when required to do Sa. Penalty on persons Cbstru-ting Streets. Restriction on Depositing Coal in certain streets. Restriction on Depositing Coal in other Streets. Carts not to be driven by any person under thirteen years of age. Prohibition of Posting Bills, &amp;c., without leave. Vehicles to have Lamps attached after sunset. Prohibition of Betting in Streets. Prohibition o 5 Unseemly Noises. Prohibition of Bad Language and Disorderly Condact. Repeal. Penalties.</p>
