        <p>PAIIPERS SENT TO GAOL. —George Mather was charged with neglecting to maintain himself whereby he became ohargfrible to the common fun I of the union on the 13th inst —Mr. B. Shearer said the prisoner wa admitted to the Workbowe on the 13th inst. He worked at Whitesross end c,nld earn 325. a week. but had lost his work through drink. That was the 4th time he had been In the Workhouse this year—Prisnner was sent to gaol for a month —3ll:thaet Morrae, 36 years of axe, an able-bodicd man, was sent to gaol for a month for a similar off snce. Monns.Y.—Before Mr. F. Monks (in the chair). Aldermen Wright: Councillors Shaw Green and Smethurst, and Mr.</p>
        <p>A N7GLECTIIII, HUSII kITD —Jame,' Murray, 15. Napier-st., 'WU charged with neglecting to maintain his wife and three ehildren,whereloy they had becorae ehargeottle to the common funds of the Werr,ngton Union.—'r. B. Shearer proseceted ea behalf of the guardians. He said that prisoner's wife and three children were admitted to the workhouse on Friday. Prieoner wes a joiner and had leen employed by Mr. Davies. but be had lost his work through drink, and had done no- thing for the past six weeks. ccarinct had been ex- treme! r hid. and he (Mr. Shearer) was instrunted to press the case. —Priscneer was sent to gaol for a Imuth with hard labour. A VirmstraLut r Tnernita.—Robert Roberts, a Welshman. was charged with travelling from Manchester to Warrington on the. London and North-Western Railway on Saturday afternoon without having a ticket, with intent to avoid pay- ing the fare.—William Treyett, a porter 4t Bank Qnay Station said that at 3.42 on Saturday afternoon a gentleman was entering a second class compartment in the train which had arrived from Manchester when he ealled his (witness's) atten- tion to the compartment. He said there was someone under `the seat. Witness went into the compartment and found prisoner under the seat. fie said lie had not got a ticket; he had come irons Manchester and wee going to Pen- maenmawr. He took him to the detective', ornce.—Deteetive Howells said he afterwards said that his ganger at Manchester bought him a ticket and he had lost it. Witness telegraphed</p>
