        <p>USEFUL PRESENTS of every defierlption, See Win- dow.-4. S. GABLLiin Ironmonger. B School Board Meeting-. A meeting of ttie Great Sankey Scnool Board was held at the schools on Tuesdn) evening, when there were present—Me.srs. Halton (chairman). Wright, and Perks, Mr 4hearer (school attendance officer), Mr G Clarke (scho)lcnaater), and NIT- Jeans (clerk). Mr. Shearer alluded to the new Education and Em- ployment of Children Act which will come into force on Janualy lst.—The Schoolmaster reported that there had been no improvement in the attend- ance of the children who had been absent through infectious diseases. Sickness of a general character, such a. sore throats, hat increa.el. The average attendance for the, nast month was 217-7 whilst the fees amounted to £2 03 21.</p>
