        <p>latckriet VG APPLICIITION.—John Worst applied for temporary authority to sell at an off-licensed hones No. 174. Knutsford-road, in lien of Alargaret Lake.—Grant.d. ALteanD TrizFr —lilizabeth Humphries, Buckley's-yard, was charged with stealing from the doorway of the sh pof Mrs Susanna Norm .n. 7r3 Winwick st.eet at five o'clock on Tuesday afternoon, two shawls. vat te is 91—The Chief Con- stable asked for a remand in 0, der to make incioiries about the prisoner, as a nnatber of pawnthriets for various articles, supposed to have been at )len. had been found in her posses- sion. Mrs Norman. who carried on business at 76,Winwick- street had some shawls at the door of her shop on Tuesday, and they were seen safe at one o'clock by her assistant. About live o'clock the assistant's attention was attracted to the prisoner, who was loitering about the premists in a suspicious manner. Shortly afterwards the assistant went to the door and missed the two shawls and at the same time missed the prisoner. Information was eiven to the police, and shortly before ten o'clock last night Superintendent Monaghan visited the prisoner's house in Buedcley'slard, where he found the two shawls in a bag. He accused prisoner of having stolen them and she admitted having done so. She was taken to the Police Station and locked up. On being searched a large number of pawatickets were found upon her. —She was remanded until this morning (Saturday).</p>
